  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "2 Kings",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 13,
    "summary": "Jehoahaz and his successors reign in wickedness in Israel—Elisha prophesies that Joash will defeat Syria—Elisha dies—A dead Israelite is restored to life after touching Elisha’s bones.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "In the three and twentieth year of Joash the son of Ahaziah king of Judah Jehoahaz the son of Jehu began to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned seventeen years.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 138,
            "end": 149
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 13:1",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And he did that which was evil in the sight of the Lord, and followed the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, which made Israel to sin; he departed not therefrom.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 14:16; 2 Kgs. 10:29; 14:24; 15:9 (9, 18, 24)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 13:2",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And the anger of the Lord was kindled against Israel, and he delivered them into the hand of Hazael king of Syria, and into the hand of Ben-hadad the son of Hazael, all their days.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
